{"type":"message","id":"419cefdb","parentId":"0db006df","timestamp":"2026-02-03T18:35:45.107Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Tue 2026-02-03 18:35 UTC] ## Mission: Full Gamma Takeoff → Populated Excel Bid Sheet\n\n**Project:** Bellevue Hospital Fire Pump & Standpipe Replacement (Project #11202205)\n**Location:** `/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/projects/Bellevue - Standpipe/`\n\n### Your Deliverable\nA completed Excel bid sheet (`takeoff/Bellevue_Standpipe_Bid_COMPLETED.xlsx`) with all 95 items populated with quantities, units, confidence scores, and notes.\n\n### Source Data\n- **Bid items:** `extraction/bid-items.json` (95 items mapped to 7 experts)\n- **Original template:** `documents/bid/Bellevue - Standpipe - 11202205_Bid Breakdown_20250313.xlsx`\n- **Drawings:** `documents/drawings/` (15 PDF files, ~150MB total)\n- **Key drawings:** Part7 contains FP sheets (FP-001 through FP-122+)\n\n### Methodology: Gamma (Hybrid)\nRun BOTH passes and cross-validate:\n\n**Alpha Pass (Bid-First):**\nFor each of the 95 bid items → search drawings/specs → extract quantity\n\n**Beta Pass (Doc-First):**\nScan each drawing set → extract all countable elements → map to bid items\n\n**Cross-Validation:**\n- Where Alpha ≠ Beta → flag discrepancy, investigate, pick best estimate\n- Where both agree → high confidence\n- Where neither found → generate RFI, mark as \"TBD\" with note\n\n### Vision Analysis\nUse Claude Sonnet for drawing analysis (API key at `~/.openclaw/credentials/anthropic-api-key`).\n- Extract: counts, dimensions, equipment tags, pipe sizes, valve counts\n- Focus areas: FP drawings for standpipes/fire pumps, Mech for HVAC, Elec for panels/circuits\n\n### Key Items to Nail (Fire Protection 43-51)\n- Item 44: Pipe linear feet (LF)\n- Item 45: Valve count (EA)\n- Item 49: Standpipes (we found 6 locations across 23 floors)\n- Item 51: Fire pumps (EA)\n\n### Expert Distribution\n- GC: 20 items (1-20)\n- Structural: 3 items (21-23)\n- Architectural: 15 items (24-25, 30-42)\n- Fire Protection: 13 items (26-29, 43-51)\n- Plumbing: 8 items (52-59)\n- Mechanical: 19 items (60-78)\n- Electrical: 17 items (79-95)\n\n### Output Format (Excel columns)\n| Item # | CSI Section | Description | Quantity | Unit | Confidence | Method | Notes/RFIs |\n\n### When Complete\n1. Save Excel to `takeoff/Bellevue_Standpipe_Bid_COMPLETED.xlsx`\n2. Save detailed analysis to `takeoff/gamma-analysis-report.md`\n3. Report back with: total confidence score, items completed vs TBD, key findings, any RFIs generated\n\nGo deep. Be thorough. Doug is excited to see the results."}],"timestamp":1770143745105}}
