{"type":"message","id":"8e117af7","parentId":"1a495887","timestamp":"2026-02-03T18:37:12.013Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01L145RxgcKB26ZYRdpLWC6w","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"B.\n\nWhere riser control or section valves are located outside of a required stair enclosure,\nthe valves shall be of such type and so installed so as to be remotely operated by an\nelectric motor. The remote control shall be from either the entrance floor or from the\nfire pump room. Operating devices shall be grouped, suitably housed, and kept locked\nwith a Fire Department lock and key. The door of the housing shall be embossed to\nindicate the purpose of the device. Instructions for operating the remote valves by the\ncontrol device shall be legible, detailed, and complete, and shall be permanently\nsecured to the inner face of the door.\n1.\nElectric Motor Operator for Butterfly Valve shall be similar to Kennedy Valve\nElectric Motor Operator, provided with an auxiliary handwheel operator for\nmanual operation. Rated for 300 psi. 120 volts. Normally open. Slow Opening\nand closing time rated for Fire Protection usage\n2.\nMotorized Valves:\na.\nManufacturers:\n1)\nLimitorque:\na)\nRemote-operated motorized control valves (ROMCV’s) shall\nbe provided on the standpipe system where indicated on the\nConstruction Documents. The ROMCV’s shall allow the Fire\nDepartment to isolate and control water flow through the\nrisers from the Fire Command Station at the entrance floor or\nfrom a Fire Pump Room.\nb.\nThe ROMCV’s shall consist of a remotely controlled isolation valve with a\nFactory Mutual-approved electric motor actuator.\nc.\nThe ROMCV’s shall be controlled (opened and closed) via Limitorque\ncontrol station system model CS/CSE. All operating devices shall be\nsuitably housed and kept locked with a fire department lock and key.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 2\nVALVES FOR FIRE SUPPRESSION\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\n21 05 04 - 5\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nd.\n\ne.\n\nf.\ng.\nh.\n\ni.\n\nj.\n--\nB.\n\nWhere riser control or section valves are located outside of a required stair enclosure,\nthe valves shall be of such type and so installed so as to be remotely operated by an\nelectric motor. The remote control shall be from either the entrance floor or from the\nfire pump room. Operating devices shall be grouped, suitably housed, and kept locked\nwith a Fire Department lock and key. The door of the housing shall be embossed to\nindicate the purpose of the device. Instructions for operating the remote valves by the\ncontrol device shall be legible, detailed, and complete, and shall be permanently\nsecured to the inner face of the door.\n1.\nElectric Motor Operator for Butterfly Valve shall be similar to Kennedy Valve\nElectric Motor Operator, provided with an auxiliary handwheel operator for\nmanual operation. Rated for 300 psi. 120 volts. Normally open. Slow Opening\nand closing time rated for Fire Protection usage\n2.\nMotorized Valves:\na.\nManufacturers:\n1)\nLimitorque:\na)\nRemote-operated motorized control valves (ROMCV’s) shall\nbe provided on the standpipe system where indicated on the\nConstruction Documents. The ROMCV’s shall allow the Fire\nDepartment to isolate and control water flow through the\nrisers from the Fire Command Station at the entrance floor or\nfrom a Fire Pump Room.\nb.\nThe ROMCV’s shall consist of a remotely controlled isolation valve with a\nFactory Mutual-approved electric motor actuator.\nc.\nThe ROMCV’s shall be controlled (opened and closed) via Limitorque\ncontrol station system model CS/CSE. All operating devices shall be\nsuitably housed and kept locked with a fire department lock and key.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 3\nVALVES FOR FIRE SUPPRESSION\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\n21 05 04 - 5\nProject No. 26-2112-000"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":2607,"aggregated":"B.\n\nWhere riser control or section valves are located outside of a required stair enclosure,\nthe valves shall be of such type and so installed so as to be remotely operated by an\nelectric motor. The remote control shall be from either the entrance floor or from the\nfire pump room. Operating devices shall be grouped, suitably housed, and kept locked\nwith a Fire Department lock and key. The door of the housing shall be embossed to\nindicate the purpose of the device. Instructions for operating the remote valves by the\ncontrol device shall be legible, detailed, and complete, and shall be permanently\nsecured to the inner face of the door.\n1.\nElectric Motor Operator for Butterfly Valve shall be similar to Kennedy Valve\nElectric Motor Operator, provided with an auxiliary handwheel operator for\nmanual operation. Rated for 300 psi. 120 volts. Normally open. Slow Opening\nand closing time rated for Fire Protection usage\n2.\nMotorized Valves:\na.\nManufacturers:\n1)\nLimitorque:\na)\nRemote-operated motorized control valves (ROMCV’s) shall\nbe provided on the standpipe system where indicated on the\nConstruction Documents. The ROMCV’s shall allow the Fire\nDepartment to isolate and control water flow through the\nrisers from the Fire Command Station at the entrance floor or\nfrom a Fire Pump Room.\nb.\nThe ROMCV’s shall consist of a remotely controlled isolation valve with a\nFactory Mutual-approved electric motor actuator.\nc.\nThe ROMCV’s shall be controlled (opened and closed) via Limitorque\ncontrol station system model CS/CSE. All operating devices shall be\nsuitably housed and kept locked with a fire department lock and key.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 2\nVALVES FOR FIRE SUPPRESSION\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\n21 05 04 - 5\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nd.\n\ne.\n\nf.\ng.\nh.\n\ni.\n\nj.\n--\nB.\n\nWhere riser control or section valves are located outside of a required stair enclosure,\nthe valves shall be of such type and so installed so as to be remotely operated by an\nelectric motor. The remote control shall be from either the entrance floor or from the\nfire pump room. Operating devices shall be grouped, suitably housed, and kept locked\nwith a Fire Department lock and key. The door of the housing shall be embossed to\nindicate the purpose of the device. Instructions for operating the remote valves by the\ncontrol device shall be legible, detailed, and complete, and shall be permanently\nsecured to the inner face of the door.\n1.\nElectric Motor Operator for Butterfly Valve shall be similar to Kennedy Valve\nElectric Motor Operator, provided with an auxiliary handwheel operator for\nmanual operation. Rated for 300 psi. 120 volts. Normally open. Slow Opening\nand closing time rated for Fire Protection usage\n2.\nMotorized Valves:\na.\nManufacturers:\n1)\nLimitorque:\na)\nRemote-operated motorized control valves (ROMCV’s) shall\nbe provided on the standpipe system where indicated on the\nConstruction Documents. The ROMCV’s shall allow the Fire\nDepartment to isolate and control water flow through the\nrisers from the Fire Command Station at the entrance floor or\nfrom a Fire Pump Room.\nb.\nThe ROMCV’s shall consist of a remotely controlled isolation valve with a\nFactory Mutual-approved electric motor actuator.\nc.\nThe ROMCV’s shall be controlled (opened and closed) via Limitorque\ncontrol station system model CS/CSE. All operating devices shall be\nsuitably housed and kept locked with a fire department lock and key.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nAlternate 3\nVALVES FOR FIRE SUPPRESSION\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\n21 05 04 - 5\nProject No. 26-2112-000","cwd":"/home/ec2-user/clawd"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770143832005}}
